{
  "comprehensible": "At the very last moment, he lost his nerve and betrayed his colleagues by shifting the blame onto them.",
  "glosses": [
    {
      "expression": "bottled it",
      "gloss": "lost his nerve and failed to do what he was supposed to do"
    },
    {
      "expression": "threw his colleagues under the bus",
      "gloss": "betrayed his colleagues to protect himself, by putting the blame on them"
    }
  ],
  "grammar": null,
  "translation": "他在最后一刻临阵退缩，还把责任推给了同事。"
}

{
  "comprehensible": "The house was in a state of dignified but shabby decline, because the people who lived there had moved away to mainland Europe a long time ago.",
  "glosses": [
    {
      "expression": "genteel decay",
      "gloss": "a kind of decline that still keeps a respectable, upper-class appearance"
    },
    {
      "expression": "having long since repaired to",
      "gloss": "having moved to (a place) a long time ago"
    },
    {
      "expression": "the Continent",
      "gloss": "mainland Europe (used especially by British speakers)"
    }
  ],
  "grammar": "The phrase 'its occupants having long since repaired to the Continent' is a participial clause that gives the reason for the house's decay. It does not have a subject-verb structure like a normal clause; 'having repaired' means 'because they had moved'.",
  "translation": "这栋房子处于一种体面而破败的状态，因为它的住户早已移居到欧洲大陆去了。"
}

{
